From: Viktor Semenov <suit.uanic@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:47:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/45] Send the production lists' state in the Specula feed

The GUI greys a trainable or researchable item by its owner's state:
requirements, entity limits and the modified cost. A viewer cannot
derive that from the feed, so the Trainer and Researcher sample now
evaluates each item for the owner as the GUI does (GetTemplateData,
AreRequirementsMet, a port of getEntityLimitAndCount, GetTechnologyData
times the researcher's cost multiplier, CheckTechnologyRequirements).
Kind 17 interns a list with each item's string, flags (requirements
met, hidden, pair top), the count that can still be added and the
costs. Pairs become two entries. Kind 12 groups 262144 (trainable) and
524288 (researchable) name the list; new group bits, so the feed stays
v14 and kind 13's plain lists go.
